*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* calculator-1-match.sno — arithmetic-expression pattern match ONLY, Variant 1:
* RIGHT recursion (the grammar of calculator-1.sno with every semantic action
* stripped).  Whole file in memory, ONE BIG MATCH, zero side effects (no
* captures, no deferred CALLS — the *X/*F/*T deferred VARIABLES are the parse
* structure itself, not side effects).  The subject is the entire input: a
* run of newline-terminated expression lines, ARBNO(X eol), anchored
* POS(0)..RPOS(0), so the match recognizes every line or fails as a whole.
*
* Atoms A (lowercase letters, unsigned ints, parens), signed factors F (unary
* sign chains via *F), terms T ('*' '/', right recursive), expressions X
* ('+' '-', right recursive).  Language recognized is identical to
* calculator-2-match; only the grammar SHAPE differs (right recursion here vs
* ARBNO iteration in -2), which is what makes the two useful as distinct
* pattern-engine stress cases.  Shares calculator.input / calculator-gen.py
* with the calculator-1/-2 evaluators.
* Run: sbl -b calculator-1-match.sno < calculator.input
*      snobol4 -b -f -d 8m -P 4m -S 4m calculator-1-match.sno < calculator.input
*      scrip --run calculator-1-match.sno < calculator.input
*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        V              =  ANY('abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz')
        I              =  SPAN('0123456789')
        A              =  V | I | '(' *X ')'
        F              =  A | '+' *F | '-' *F
        T              =  F '*' *T | F '/' *T | F
        X              =  T '+' *X | T '-' *X | T
        eol            =  CHAR(10)
        C              =  POS(0) ARBNO(X eol) RPOS(0)
*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        &TRIM          =  0
*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*  ONE READ — SPITBOL raw mode: -f0 attaches stdin, -r sets raw record length;
*  newlines come back in-string, short read at EOF (manual, file processing)
        INPUT(.INPUT, 9, '[-f0 -r4000000]')
        src            =  INPUT                          :F(fail)
        src            C                                 :F(fail)
        OUTPUT         =  'matched bytes=' SIZE(src)      :(END)
fail    OUTPUT         =  'Pattern match failed'
*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
END
